    "recommendations": "• Mark the main driveway entrance and the access drive entrance with reflective address numbers visible from the road in both directions.\n• Keep the circular driveway clear of parked vehicles so responding units can complete a full loop and exit without backing.\n• Trim vegetation along the access drive to maintain clearance for emergency vehicles on both sides and overhead.\n• Cut back dense vegetation that runs close to the main residence and detached structure to create open ground between the plants and the building walls.\n• Mark which driveway or access point provides the most direct route to each structure so responders can identify the correct approach quickly on arrival.\n• Keep the access drive surface in passable condition for heavy emergency vehicles.\n• Confirm that the detached structure has a visible address marker or unit identifier posted at its entrance.\n• Remove or thin dense shrubs or trees that block sightlines between the road and the structures, so responders can visually assess conditions on approach.\n• Identify a clear staging area within the circular driveway or vehicle parking area and keep it free of stored equipment, vehicles, or landscaping features that would prevent multiple units from positioning simultaneously."
